  "_": [
    "Island Haven, first pass: the numbers the game's code already places things at,",
    "written as ranges so they can be checked against the file rather than trusted.",
    "Blender coordinates: X east, Y north-south, Z height. Every range is in studs.",
    "A tolerance is a stated tolerance, not a rounding accident: where the brief gave",
    "an exact number the range is tight, and where it gave a shape the range is the",
    "room that shape needs.",
    "",
    "The plots carry no top_z. Their pads are flat at 6.5 but each also wears a lip",
    "and four fence posts a side, so the highest point of the OBJECT is the top of a",
    "post, not the surface furniture stands on. A bounding box cannot tell those",
    "apart, so claiming to check it here would be a check that proves nothing."
